  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "The Twin Pillars of Software Quality: A Deep Dive into Testing and Debugging\nIn
    the world of software development, writing code is often the easiest part of
    the job. The true challenge lies in ensuring that the code does exactly what
    it is intended to do\u2014and nothing more. This is where Testing and Debugging
    come into play. While the terms are often used interchangeably by laypeople,
    they represent two distinct, yet inextricably linked, phases of the development
    lifecycle.\n\n1. Software Testing: The Search for Truth\nTesting is the proactive
    process of executing a program with the intent of finding errors. It is a systematic
    exploration of a system's boundaries to ensure it meets its requirements.\n\nIn
    a modern \"Shift-Left\" environment, testing happens as early as possible. We
    categorize testing into several layers, often visualized as a Testing Pyramid:\n\nUnit
    Testing: The foundation. Developers write small scripts to test individual functions
    or classes in isolation. If a \"calculateTax\" function fails, you know exactly
    where the logic broke.\n\nIntegration Testing: This ensures that different modules
    or services work together. A unit test might show that the database client works
    and the API works, but an integration test ensures the API can actually talk
    to the database.\n\n\n\n\n\n"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
